{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"0b94dcc10a9eda81f4ecef1e5776bfec2dad0453cf8f632ad3743ddd00af4e01","packTokens":2621,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":2541,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when its status in the existing system is in the configured open-status list (default ['open']), it has a due date, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold is the default 7, business time zone Europe/London, the injected clock set to 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then the call for the invoice due 2026-10-08 returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7, and the call for the invoice due 2026-10-09 returns overdue = false and daysOverdue = 6\",\n    \"Given threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-07, 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-05 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then the calls return overdue = false for the invoices due 2026-10-07 and 2026-10-06, and overdue = true for the invoice due 2026-10-05\",\n    \"Given threshold 7, default open-status list ['open'], and seven invoices each 20 days past due with statuses paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed and credited when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then every call returns overdue = false\",\n    \"Given threshold 7 and an invoice with status 'open' and a null due date when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for it then the call returns overdue = false and throws no exception\",\n    \"Given business time zone Europe/London, default threshold, and an open invoice due 2026-09-01 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called at instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local), then at 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local) then the first call returns daysOverdue = 6 and overdue = false, and the second returns daysOverdue = 7 and overdue = true\",\n    \"Given an open invoice due 6 days ago is not in the overdue list response, and no job or data change runs when the injected clock moves forward 1 day and the overdue list is requested again then the response now holds the invoice with daysOverdue = 7, and the invoice record in the existing database is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue (calendar days since the due date).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, and in the existing database: open invoice A for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 due 2026-10-01, open invoice B due 2026-10-12, invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid, and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status cancelled when an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list then the response is 200 and holds only invoice A, with its invoice number, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14\",\n    \"Given invoice A is in the overdue list when its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again then invoice A is no longer in the response and no overdue flag was written to the invoice record\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given customer X has 2 overdue invoices, customer Y has 1 overdue invoice, and customer Z has none when an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with customerId = X, then with customerId = Z then the first response holds exactly customer X's 2 invoices and the second response is 200 with an empty list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside the named fixed bucket (7–30, 31–60 or 61+, limits inclusive, not shifted by the configured overdue threshold), or respond 400 with a validation error when the bucket value is not one of these.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given default threshold 7 and overdue invoices at 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90 days overdue when the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30, then 31–60, then 61+ then the responses hold {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61, 90}\",\n    \"Given customers X and Y each have overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days when the overdue list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31–60, then with customerId = X and bucket 7–30 then the first response holds only X's 45-day invoice and the second holds only X's 10-day invoice\",\n    \"Given any overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6' then the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter\",\n    \"Given the overdue threshold is set to 5 and an open invoice is 6 days past due when the overdue list is requested without a bucket, then with bucket 7–30, 31–60 and 61+ then the invoice is in the unfiltered response and is in none of the three bucket responses\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no token, and separately an expired token when the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without customer and bucket filters then each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body\",\n    \"Given a valid token for any staff user with no special role when the overdue list endpoint is called then the response is 200, not 401 or 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint carries a valid, unexpired token from the existing API whose principal is not a staff user, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 403 without returning invoice or customer data or changing data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a valid, unexpired token issued by the existing API for a principal without the staff marker (for example a service/integration client or a non-staff user account) when the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without customer and bucket filters then each response is 403 and its body holds no invoice or customer data\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The overdue list endpoint meets the stated latency at the stated data volumes, with or without filters.\",\n  \"Customer PII (billing email addresses) and invoice amounts are kept out of application logs.\",\n  \"All Invoice Reminders endpoints require staff authentication.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}